asr-000282
00:40:29.890 --> 00:40:36.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: Kami po sa Pinoy Workers is very supportive of our fisherfolk and farmers in the West Philippine Sea.

asr-000283
00:40:36.890 --> 00:40:41.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: Dahil po ako personal taga-Palawan po ako, kaya this is close to our heart po.

asr-000284
00:40:41.890 --> 00:40:48.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: And yung katanungan lang po for the fishing communities in Palawan, particularly those dependent on the fishing grounds in our West Philippine Sea,

asr-000285
00:40:48.890 --> 00:40:54.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: what livelihood and production support will be available in this coming budget...

asr-000286
00:40:54.890 --> 00:40:56.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: in the 2027 budget?

asr-000287
00:40:56.890 --> 00:41:07.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: And how does BEFAR, if that is the case, plan to improve access to assistance such as fuel, ice, fishing gear, insurance, and market support?

asr-000288
00:41:07.890 --> 00:41:08.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: Thank you po.

asr-000289
00:41:08.890 --> 00:41:18.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, sa Palawan, meron tayong bagong port na ginagawa ng Philippine Fisheries Development Authority sa Puerto Princesa area, no?

asr-000290
00:41:18.890 --> 00:41:19.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Near Puerto Princesa.

asr-000291
00:41:19.890 --> 00:41:22.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: That will be 15 hectare yata na port.

asr-000292
00:41:22.890 --> 00:41:29.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: 15 hectare yata na port na lalagyan natin ng ice plant, cold storage, blast freezers.

asr-000293
00:41:29.890 --> 00:41:33.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At ikokonek yon sa other side sa Ulugan Bay.

asr-000294
00:41:33.890 --> 00:41:41.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Para nga yung mga isda from the West Philippine Sea, ibabawa sa Ulugan Bay na port din na meron tayo doon.

asr-000295
00:41:41.890 --> 00:41:48.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Para tas itatransport nalang by land to that port, that new port, which should be finished by next year.

asr-000296
00:41:48.890 --> 00:41:50.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Para ma-process yon at madala sa mga iba-ibang market.

asr-000298
00:41:52.890 --> 00:41:53.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Number one, no?

asr-000299
00:41:53.890 --> 00:41:57.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tuloy-tuloy yung ating intervention sa seaweed.

asr-000300
00:41:57.890 --> 00:42:11.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Magtatayo tayo ng bagong bioreactor facility rin by this year, hopefully, for planting material, propagation of planting material sa seaweed sa Palawan.

asr-000301
00:42:11.890 --> 00:42:16.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron na tayo sa Sorsogon, may Palawan tayo, at meron pa isang location, I forgot lang kung saan.

asr-000302
00:42:16.890 --> 00:42:21.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But Palawan is, definitely we want to increase yung seaweed production natin sa Palawan para yung mga mga isda,

asr-000303
00:42:21.890 --> 00:42:25.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: pwede rin mag-aalaga ng kanilang seaweeds.

asr-000304
00:42:25.890 --> 00:42:36.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron din tayong livestock program na ipapamahagi like mga kambing at tupa sa mga fisher folks na may spare time sila after fishing sa madaling araw.

asr-000305
00:42:36.890 --> 00:42:41.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pwede rin sila mag-aalaga ng hayop for their own communities, Mr. Chair.

asr-000306
00:42:41.890 --> 00:42:50.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: Ano lang po, Mr. Secretary, regarding po kayo sa cold storage, meron po kayang possibility na magkaroon tayo ng cold storage facilities?

asr-000307
00:42:50.890 --> 00:42:59.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: Kasi po, sa mga communities po na nalagayan namin sa west coast, especially po sa mga barangay ng Apurawan, yun po sa Aboyland in Puerto,

asr-000308
00:42:59.890 --> 00:43:10.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: yung reklamo po ng mga fisher folk, dahil nga walang cold storage na available para sa kanila, usually naubos na yung catch nila galing sa laot kasi nabibili ng mga buyers na nandun na sa Palawate.

asr-000309
00:43:10.890 --> 00:43:18.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: At di na nila nabababa sa Palawan mainland yung catch. At yung nagsasuffer po yung local economy kasi nga nababawasan na po yung availability ng fish.

asr-000310
00:43:20.890 --> 00:43:27.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: Kaya meron po kayang provisions po for the budget to allocate for cold storage?

asr-000311
00:43:27.890 --> 00:43:37.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: For 2027, Mr. Chair, meron kaming nasa budget namin na solar-powered ice plants na 5 to 10 tons per day na capacity.

asr-000312
00:43:37.890 --> 00:43:42.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron kaming 10 to 15, depende sa capacity na units.

asr-000313
00:43:42.890 --> 00:43:47.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And medyo, ilan dun mapupunta talaga sa Palawan.

asr-000314
00:43:47.890 --> 00:43:48.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Kasi nga, yung North Palawan saka Southern Palawan, meron kaming 10 to 15 units.

asr-000317
00:43:50.890 --> 00:43:51.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung North Palawan, kailangan may mga ice plant.

asr-000318
00:43:51.890 --> 00:44:01.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tapos yung cold storage and freezers nandun sa gitna, dun sa may Puerto Princesa para yung fresh fish or seafoods nama may yelo,

asr-000319
00:44:01.890 --> 00:44:07.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: madadala natin sa blast freezing area, cold storage areas para ma-process.

asr-000320
00:44:07.890 --> 00:44:11.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And madala sa tourist markets itin atin in Manila and everywhere.

asr-000321
00:44:11.890 --> 00:44:13.890
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ayun po yung general plan, Mr. Chair.

asr-000322
00:44:13.890 --> 00:44:15.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: Thank you po, Mr. Chair.

asr-000323
00:44:15.890 --> 00:44:17.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: And that's for us po.

asr-000324
00:44:17.890 --> 00:44:19.890
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: We just wanted

asr-000325
00:44:19.890 --> 00:44:25.350
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: to express and manifest our support to the agency and

asr-000326
00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:30.030
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: hopefully we could empower our fishing and farmer communities more in the

asr-000327
00:44:30.030 --> 00:44:35.650
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: coming budget. And nandito ang aming

asr-000328
00:44:35.650 --> 00:44:39.990
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: pong tanggapan, nandito po upang magbigay ng mas maigting na suporta po para

asr-000329
00:44:39.990 --> 00:44:43.950
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: sa ating mga kapwang manggagawa. Thank you very much, Mr. Chair, for the time and all the best po to the department and Mr.

asr-000330
00:44:43.950 --> 00:44:55.340
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Secretary, thank you po. Thank you, Congressman Carl, and Secretary, for the

asr-000331
00:44:55.340 --> 00:44:59.540
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: second round from the minority

asr-000332
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:31.310
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Representative Sarah Elago, Representative Brian Poe, Representative Cocoy Salvador, Representative Keith Flores, Representative Steve Solon,

asr-000333
00:45:31.310 --> 00:45:54.700
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Rep. Chagavaria, Rep. Kukuyap, Rep. Antonio Romano III, Rep. Nicolas Casi, Rep. Luigi Villapuerte,

asr-000334
00:45:54.700 --> 00:46:02.480
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Rep. Renante Agurgancia, Deputy Speaker Janet Garin,

asr-000335
00:46:03.200 --> 00:46:09.140
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: and the first round, Representative Howard Guintu.

asr-000336
00:46:14.140 --> 00:46:20.120
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Thank you, Mr. Chair, and to the DA family, good evening.

asr-000337
00:46:21.320 --> 00:46:24.220
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Pasensya na po, alam ko po nga kumakain po kayo.

asr-000338
00:46:25.880 --> 00:46:32.260
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: I would just like to ask, actually my question is directed to PFDA, Mr. Chair.

asr-000339
00:46:32.540 --> 00:46:37.120
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: May I know how much is the funding allocation for the construction of fish ports

asr-000340
00:46:37.640 --> 00:46:40.340
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: for 2027 NEP?

asr-000341
00:46:51.840 --> 00:46:52.400
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Fish port

asr-000342
00:46:55.750 --> 00:46:57.130
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Good evening, Mr. Chair.

asr-000343
00:46:57.670 --> 00:47:06.110
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Magkano po yung budget na nilagay natin, or ang budget na meron para sa mga fish ports natin for 2027?

asr-000344
00:47:06.450 --> 00:47:12.210
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Actually, ang nasama po sa NEP is 3.8.

asr-000345
00:47:12.730 --> 00:47:13.510
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Magkano po?

asr-000346
00:47:13.790 --> 00:47:15.010
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: 3.8 billion.

asr-000347
00:47:15.010 --> 00:47:17.010
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: 3.8 billion.

asr-000348
00:47:17.330 --> 00:47:20.970
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: From this 3.8 billion, magkano po ang naka-allocate sa atin?

asr-000349
00:47:20.990 --> 00:47:22.590
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Sa ating mga ongoing projects?

asr-000350
00:47:25.870 --> 00:47:28.830
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Yung 2.1 po.

asr-000351
00:47:29.070 --> 00:47:33.070
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: 2.1 sa ongoing, so yung remaining para sa mga...

asr-000352
00:47:33.070 --> 00:47:34.130
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Deepwater.

asr-000353
00:47:34.510 --> 00:47:39.470
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: For new projects or new proposed fish ports. Tama po?

asr-000354
00:47:39.750 --> 00:47:41.750
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Sa deepwater po yung balansa po.

asr-000355
00:47:42.590 --> 00:47:45.790
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Yes, fish ports po. Deepwater.

asr-000356
00:47:46.390 --> 00:47:51.790
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Pero ang ano po, ilan po doon sa 3.8 billion na binigay po ng...

asr-000357
00:47:52.970 --> 00:47:58.450
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: DBM, ilan po doon sa lumang project, ilan po ang sa bago?

asr-000358
00:48:02.030 --> 00:48:03.590
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Lahat po sa ongoing po yun.

asr-000359
00:48:03.730 --> 00:48:06.490
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Ongoing. So sa bago po, wala po tayong naka-allocate.

asr-000360
00:48:07.630 --> 00:48:08.630
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Wala po pang DBM.

asr-000361
00:48:09.210 --> 00:48:11.990
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Wala po tayong pondong, hindi po tayong nabigyan.

asr-000362
00:48:12.210 --> 00:48:16.910
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Pero meron po ba tayong proposal for new fish ports?

asr-000363
00:48:17.350 --> 00:48:17.930
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Opo, opo.

asr-000364
00:48:18.850 --> 00:48:23.350
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Actually, ang total proposal po namin is 8 billion po.

asr-000365
00:48:23.350 --> 00:48:24.170
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: I'm sorry.

asr-000366
00:48:25.250 --> 00:48:25.930
Rep. Carl Nicolas C. Cari: 8 billion.

asr-000367
00:48:25.950 --> 00:48:32.010
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Ang proposed po natin for both old and new ports.

asr-000368
00:48:32.470 --> 00:48:32.910
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Opo, opo.

asr-000369
00:48:32.990 --> 00:48:37.410
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: And yet, ang nabigyan po sa atin ay 3.8 billion lang po. Tama po?

asr-000370
00:48:37.810 --> 00:48:42.570
PFDA Acting General Manager Glen A. Pangapalan: Yes, yes.

asr-000371
00:48:44.730 --> 00:48:47.090
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Mr. Chair, this is where I am concerned, no?

asr-000372
00:48:47.830 --> 00:48:54.990
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Nakita po natin na, so 2025, ang nabigay po sa PFDA, 5.5 billion.

asr-000373
00:48:55.610 --> 00:48:58.110
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Tapos po, 2026, 4.5.

asr-000374
00:48:58.110 --> 00:48:59.830
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Ngayon po, 3.8.

asr-000375
00:48:59.850 --> 00:49:04.290
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Pababa po na pababa yung pondong na-allocate po sa PFDA.

asr-000376
00:49:05.090 --> 00:49:12.670
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: And yet, kumakita natin, napakarami pong port na pangangailangan ang ating bansa

asr-000377
00:49:12.670 --> 00:49:16.190
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: because of our archipelagic nature.

asr-000378
00:49:16.530 --> 00:49:18.330
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Alam niyo po, mayroon akong research na nabasa.

asr-000379
00:49:18.530 --> 00:49:26.030
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: There's about 2,800 fishports in Japan.

asr-000380
00:49:26.030 --> 00:49:27.490
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: In Japan po.

asr-000381
00:49:27.490 --> 00:49:34.510
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Now, wherein talagang makita natin how successful the fishing industry is in Japan.

asr-000382
00:49:35.170 --> 00:49:41.250
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: However, in our country, parang wala pa po ata sa dalawang daan.

asr-000383
00:49:41.830 --> 00:49:44.790
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: O baka 100 plus lang po yung fishport natin.

asr-000384
00:49:45.050 --> 00:49:48.350
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: And yet, we have 7,000 plus islands.

asr-000385
00:49:49.070 --> 00:49:53.550
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: With that, Mr. Chair, we have members here in the appropriation.

asr-000386
00:49:53.550 --> 00:49:56.770
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Baka naman po pwede po nating tugunan.

asr-000387
00:49:56.770 --> 00:50:03.950
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Yung pangangailangan ng PFDA with regard to the variants needed in order to fulfill their mandate.

asr-000388
00:50:05.290 --> 00:50:06.310
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Marami po tayo.

asr-000389
00:50:06.390 --> 00:50:13.930
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Alam mo, hindi ko na po inaano, pero karamihan po ng pondo ng DA po na pupunta po sa ating mga magsasaka,

asr-000390
00:50:14.150 --> 00:50:15.150
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: sa ating mga farmers.

asr-000391
00:50:15.610 --> 00:50:25.110
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Parang nakakalimutan po natin na malaking tulong din at malaking portion din ng ating mga magagawa

asr-000392
00:50:25.110 --> 00:50:27.430
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: ay mga fisher folks.

asr-000393
00:50:27.690 --> 00:50:37.770
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: So, kung saan na po pwede po nating dagdagan ang pondo ng DA para po mabihayaan naman po ang ating mga fisher folks.

asr-000394
00:50:38.110 --> 00:50:42.290
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: And then, another question, Mr. Chair.

asr-000395
00:50:43.290 --> 00:50:49.750
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: In 2025, the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration, or NOAA,

asr-000396
00:50:50.790 --> 00:50:52.190
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: parang may binan po sila.

asr-000397
00:50:52.350 --> 00:50:54.330
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: They assessed the Philippine fisheries and denied.

asr-000398
00:50:54.330 --> 00:50:58.610
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: They denied comparability findings for two blue swimming crab.

asr-000399
00:50:59.470 --> 00:51:03.750
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: This is a fishery ID 2129 and fishery ID 2130.

asr-000400
00:51:04.670 --> 00:51:12.930
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: I'm just concerned regarding this particular, what do you call it, particular crab, no?

asr-000401
00:51:13.330 --> 00:51:20.730
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Kasi napakalaki nung nawawala sa atin na potential income from export

asr-000402
00:51:20.730 --> 00:51:22.730
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: just because this particular...

asr-000403
00:51:24.330 --> 00:51:29.050
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Variant is banned in the U.S.

asr-000404
00:51:30.290 --> 00:51:40.470
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Meron po ba tayong ginagawang paraan para po matulungan yung ating mga crab fisheries or racers?

asr-000405
00:51:41.690 --> 00:51:51.910
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, we would like to request Usec Drus Bayate of Fisheries for officials to give the details of the blue swimming crab issue.

asr-000406
00:51:52.410 --> 00:51:52.910
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000407
00:51:54.330 --> 00:51:55.570
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Good evening.

asr-000408
00:51:56.510 --> 00:52:00.410
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: I'm Usec Drus Bayate, Undersecretary for Fisheries.

asr-000409
00:52:01.430 --> 00:52:08.390
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Our issue with the U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration

asr-000410
00:52:08.390 --> 00:52:15.070
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: stem from the implementation of the U.S. Marine Mammal Protection Act.

asr-000411
00:52:15.070 --> 00:52:24.080
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: May import provision dun sa U.S. Marine Mammal Protection Act.

asr-000413
00:52:25.840 --> 00:52:37.120
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: At the fishing gears na ginagamit natin sa pag-capture ng crabs,

asr-000414
00:52:37.400 --> 00:52:41.260
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: ang crabs na sinasabi nila alimasag, blue swimming crabs,

asr-000415
00:52:41.840 --> 00:52:46.000
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: this is our major export to the U.S., ang blue crab meat.

asr-000416
00:52:47.380 --> 00:52:52.500
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: So, ang blue crab meat natin in the country are concentrated in the Visayan Sea,

asr-000417
00:52:52.500 --> 00:52:55.360
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: in Guimara Strait,

asr-000418
00:52:55.840 --> 00:52:57.360
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: and Malampaya Sound.

asr-000419
00:52:58.900 --> 00:53:02.620
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: So, itong mga areas na ito,

asr-000420
00:53:03.960 --> 00:53:06.940
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: may findings ang mga researchers in the past,

asr-000421
00:53:07.680 --> 00:53:13.920
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: na pag hinuhuli nila, ginagamit nila yung sinasabi mong fisheries ID.

asr-000422
00:53:14.340 --> 00:53:20.240
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: That is ang isang 2930 and 2931.

asr-000423
00:53:20.740 --> 00:53:21.940
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: 31, magkasunod.

asr-000424
00:53:21.940 --> 00:53:23.440
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: 2129 at 2130.

asr-000425
00:53:23.800 --> 00:53:24.000
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Yeah.

asr-000426
00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:24.240
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Tama po.

asr-000427
00:53:25.840 --> 00:53:31.040
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: That refers to the fishing gear na ginagamit, which is the crab gill net.

asr-000428
00:53:31.700 --> 00:53:36.500
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: At ang isa, nagre-refer sa crab pots.

asr-000429
00:53:36.780 --> 00:53:37.280
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: And traps.

asr-000430
00:53:37.560 --> 00:53:37.820
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Okay.

asr-000431
00:53:38.340 --> 00:53:45.940
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: So, in the process na nilalagay ito siya, actually, our stakeholders there are artisanal fishers.

asr-000432
00:53:45.940 --> 00:53:54.840
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: These artisanal fishers are stakeholders, na major stakeholders ng coastal municipalities.

asr-000433
00:53:55.840 --> 00:54:00.400
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: They are under the jurisdiction of the local government units.

asr-000434
00:54:00.620 --> 00:54:04.520
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: And BIFAR is committed to assist them.

asr-000435
00:54:05.380 --> 00:54:13.420
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Kasi, in the process of fishing, at maglagay sila ng kanilang gill net,

asr-000436
00:54:14.200 --> 00:54:18.180
