asr-001581
02:36:40.080 --> 02:36:46.980
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa fisher folks naman, meron kaya humingi ang increase ang BIFAR ng budget from 10 to 12 billion

asr-001582
02:36:46.980 --> 02:36:53.560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: to address din yung mga, like yung solar aerators na gusto natin at solar pumps.

asr-001583
02:36:53.740 --> 02:37:00.780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Gusto natin ibigay sa mga aquaculture, mariculture natin para nga maka-cope sila sa coming El Niño.

asr-001584
02:37:01.460 --> 02:37:02.140
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you, Sec.

asr-001585
02:37:02.220 --> 02:37:09.740
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: So, tatlo po na line items yung kailangan po natin dagdagan para po makatugon po tayo ng mas mabilis sa...

asr-001586
02:37:10.380 --> 02:37:15.300
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Kung magkaroon man po ng El Niño, yung una po, yung Presidential Assistance of Farmers and Fisher Folk.

asr-001587
02:37:15.560 --> 02:37:21.960
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Pangalawa po yung Fertilizer Assistance Fund, which as you mentioned po, 8 billion yung kakulangan.

asr-001588
02:37:21.960 --> 02:37:22.960
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Tapos yung pangatlo po, yung sa...

asr-001589
02:37:23.740 --> 02:37:26.720
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Fisher Folk sa under BIFAR.

asr-001590
02:37:27.140 --> 02:37:28.880
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: So, Sir Sec, if we may...

asr-001591
02:37:28.880 --> 02:37:34.000
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: When you submit po the prioritization of the wish list,

asr-001592
02:37:34.300 --> 02:37:40.140
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: medyo mahaba po kasi, Sec, yung wish list and being cognizant po of the limited fiscal space,

asr-001593
02:37:40.220 --> 02:37:42.600
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: we'll request for your help, Sec, to prioritize it.

asr-001594
02:37:42.940 --> 02:37:46.860
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Pero please po, Sec, if it's okay po to put as a separate category,

asr-001595
02:37:46.860 --> 02:37:51.860
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: ito yung mga pantugon sa El Niño, just so we can give...

asr-001596
02:37:53.740 --> 02:37:59.120
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: special consideration to it para po matulungan din po namin yung Department of Agriculture

asr-001597
02:37:59.120 --> 02:38:03.340
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: na mabilis na makatugon po sa pangangailangan na ating mga magsasaka dahil po sa El Niño.

asr-001598
02:38:03.840 --> 02:38:07.020
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, Madam Chair. We will supply you with all the details, Madam Chair.

asr-001599
02:38:07.200 --> 02:38:08.740
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you very much po, Sec, Kiko.

asr-001600
02:38:10.400 --> 02:38:13.260
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: That is on the part of the Department of Agriculture po.

asr-001601
02:38:13.260 --> 02:38:23.700
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: If I may po, Admin Guillen, any wish list, any items for consideration that you would like to put forth to the Committee on Appropriation?

asr-001602
02:38:23.740 --> 02:38:28.140
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Thank you po, Madam Chair and all of our members of the Congress.

asr-001603
02:38:28.700 --> 02:38:38.480
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: As we conclude this hearing, we respectfully appeal for your support, of course, in increasing NIA's FY2027 budget po.

asr-001604
02:38:39.160 --> 02:38:44.260
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: NIA requested around P233 billion but only P46 billion was included in the NEP,

asr-001605
02:38:44.660 --> 02:38:51.440
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: significantly lower po than our nearly P64 billion budget for FY2026.

asr-001606
02:38:51.440 --> 02:38:52.440
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: With this...

asr-001607
02:38:53.740 --> 02:38:57.000
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: reduction, many critical irrigation projects may be delayed,

asr-001608
02:38:57.560 --> 02:39:03.220
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: including ongoing projects that must be completed to protect the government's existing investments

asr-001609
02:39:03.220 --> 02:39:05.740
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and deliver their long-awaited benefits to farmers.

asr-001610
02:39:06.200 --> 02:39:10.200
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Kahit po yung mga congressman po kanina, Madam Chair, nagagalit po sa akin

asr-001611
02:39:10.200 --> 02:39:14.460
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: dahil substantial din po ang pag-reduce ng kanilang mga budgets.

asr-001612
02:39:15.040 --> 02:39:22.840
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: So, we also respectfully request that NIA's budget be restored to a program-based PREC-C presentation.

asr-001613
02:39:22.840 --> 02:39:31.480
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: This will give us a reasonable flexibility to address unavoidable technical right-of-way and site readiness issues

asr-001614
02:39:31.480 --> 02:39:37.000
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: while maintaining full transparency, accountability, and congressional oversight po.

asr-001615
02:39:37.360 --> 02:39:44.280
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: At a time when we must strengthen food security and prepare for the possible civil effects of El Nino and climate change,

asr-001616
02:39:44.760 --> 02:39:47.520
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: irrigation cannot be treated as an ordinary expense.

asr-001617
02:39:47.520 --> 02:39:52.720
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: It is a strategic investment in agricultural productivity, rural development,

asr-001618
02:39:52.840 --> 02:39:55.220
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: and stability of our nation's food supply.

asr-001619
02:39:55.820 --> 02:40:03.600
